1
00:00:00,418 --> 00:00:01,627
Previously on Reacher...

2
00:00:01,711 --> 00:00:03,504
She sent Anna an address.

3
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:05,339
[Russell] First floor is
an abandoned restaurant.

4
00:00:05,423 --> 00:00:07,174
Looks like it's under
some kind of renovation.

5
00:00:07,258 --> 00:00:08,551
[Reacher] That's where
we're headed to next.

6
00:00:08,634 --> 00:00:09,885
-[glass shatters]
-[grunts]

7
00:00:09,969 --> 00:00:12,012
I got a GSW to the chest!

8
00:00:12,096 --> 00:00:13,597
Check in on Russell Plum.

9
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:15,808
Tell him
I'm sorry I left him at the library.

10
00:00:15,891 --> 00:00:17,017
The night my sister died,

11
00:00:17,101 --> 00:00:20,187
she had a jump drive
with a decades-old photo.

12
00:00:20,271 --> 00:00:21,981
General Putra wants to take
a photo with the two of us.

13
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:25,443
[Ahlquist] The whiteboard was
in the background, out of focus.

14
00:00:25,526 --> 00:00:28,904
Newly developed AI can essentially
refocus the lens.

15
00:00:28,988 --> 00:00:30,030
It's working.

16
00:00:30,114 --> 00:00:31,615
[Ahlquist] It contains the formula

17
00:00:31,699 --> 00:00:33,200
for a chemical weapon
of mass destruction.

18
00:00:33,284 --> 00:00:34,201
[groans]

19
00:00:34,285 --> 00:00:35,327
You send a suicide bomber

20
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:37,538
with that stuff strapped to him
into Times Square,

21
00:00:37,621 --> 00:00:39,623
he'll kill everyone
within a ten-block radius.

22
00:00:39,707 --> 00:00:41,167
Make enough to kill thousands.

23
00:00:41,250 --> 00:00:43,669
Lila's auctioning off the drive
on the dark web

24
00:00:43,753 --> 00:00:44,920
at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

25
00:00:45,004 --> 00:00:47,173
They're gonna kill people tonight
to prove it works.

26
00:00:47,256 --> 00:00:49,884
When I said Delta hunted down
and took out General Putra,

27
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,677
I was the one who pulled the trigger.

28
00:00:51,761 --> 00:00:54,680
The woman calling herself Amisha
saw me do it.

29
00:00:55,181 --> 00:00:56,891
They're hitting here. Where are you?

30
00:00:56,974 --> 00:00:57,975
This is happening now.

31
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,268
Right now, they don't know we know.

32
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:00,936
Our best chance is
to neutralize the attack.

33
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:03,063
-How?
-[yelling]

34
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:04,982
[explosion]

35
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,151
[people screaming]

36
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:12,907
-[tense music playing]
-[siren wailing]

37
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,075
[people screaming]

38
00:01:15,159 --> 00:01:17,077
[shouting indistinctly]

39
00:01:17,161 --> 00:01:19,580
-[glass shatters]
-[screaming continues]

40
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:24,710
-[security guard] Freeze, asshole!
-[gun slide racks]

41
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:26,420
-Don't fucking move!
-[horn honking]

42
00:01:26,504 --> 00:01:28,005
[tires screeching]

43
00:01:28,088 --> 00:01:28,964
Get in!

44
00:01:29,048 --> 00:01:30,591
[exciting music playing]

45
00:01:30,674 --> 00:01:32,218
[Reacher] Go! [grunts]

46
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:34,053
[gunshots]

47
00:01:35,471 --> 00:01:36,889
[bullets thudding into van]

48
00:01:36,972 --> 00:01:38,224
What the hell happened?

49
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:40,267
Sampson tackled the bomber into the river.

50
00:01:40,351 --> 00:01:42,645
The water stopped the toxin
from aerosolizing.

51
00:01:43,813 --> 00:01:44,772
Sampson's dead.

52
00:01:45,523 --> 00:01:46,440
Shit.

53
00:01:46,524 --> 00:01:48,150
He saved a lot of lives.

54
00:01:48,234 --> 00:01:49,235
[Reacher] Temporarily.

55
00:01:49,318 --> 00:01:51,362
No one's gonna buy that bomb
unless they see that it works.

56
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:53,280
Lila and Amisha will try again.

57
00:01:53,364 --> 00:01:54,615
And we have no idea where.

58
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:56,534
Tomorrow's morning commute,
like we thought.

59
00:01:57,243 --> 00:01:58,911
Maybe something else.

60
00:01:58,994 --> 00:02:00,746
I don't know, but it's gonna happen soon.

61
00:02:00,830 --> 00:02:02,414
We have to tell someone.

62
00:02:02,498 --> 00:02:04,625
Who? They're gonna blame us for this.

63
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:05,835
We're at the site of the bombing

64
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:07,711
and then take off in a van
after we sent all those cops

65
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:08,796
to the concert for nothing?

66
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,673
They're gonna think
we did that as a distraction.

67
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,132
We got to ditch this van.

68
00:02:12,216 --> 00:02:14,093
[suspenseful music playing]

69
00:02:14,176 --> 00:02:15,678
Find me a busy restaurant.

70
00:02:15,761 --> 00:02:18,472
-[horn honks]
-[horn honks]

71
00:02:19,473 --> 00:02:21,475
-[indistinct chatter]
-[siren wailing]

72
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:23,561
-[indistinct radio chatter]
-[helicopter whirring]

73
00:02:25,062 --> 00:02:28,148
Ma'am, we're gonna need
to get you out of here

74
00:02:28,232 --> 00:02:29,817
in case of a second attack.

75
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,902
[melancholy music playing]

76
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:36,448
There was a crew
shooting video of the event.

77
00:02:37,575 --> 00:02:39,994
I want to see every frame
before the police get ahold of it.

78
00:02:42,371 --> 00:02:45,207
We don't know who we can trust,
and I'm not gonna let anyone bury this.

79
00:02:48,043 --> 00:02:49,712
We're gonna find who killed John...

80
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,966
...and we're gonna make them fucking pay.

81
00:03:09,481 --> 00:03:10,608
[car alarm chirps]

82
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,446
[Tamara] It's been too long.

83
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:16,947
I don't like him doing this.

84
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:19,909
He's least likely to draw attention.

85
00:03:20,868 --> 00:03:22,578
He's small-town, but he's capable.

86
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:24,830
You know he intends
to kill Lila and Amisha,

87
00:03:24,914 --> 00:03:26,457
or whatever the hell
their names really are.

88
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:27,875
Good.

89
00:03:27,958 --> 00:03:29,293
Better world without 'em.

90
00:03:30,502 --> 00:03:32,630
Yeah, well...

91
00:03:32,713 --> 00:03:34,798
it's hard to go back to Mayfield
after you body someone,

92
00:03:34,882 --> 00:03:36,300
even if they deserve it.

93
00:03:36,383 --> 00:03:38,010
They already killed Anna and Ben.

94
00:03:38,886 --> 00:03:40,262
They shouldn't get to take his life, too.

95
00:03:40,346 --> 00:03:42,097
I didn't want him involved
in the first place.

96
00:03:42,181 --> 00:03:43,474
[vehicle approaches]

97
00:03:44,016 --> 00:03:44,934
[Reacher] That's him.

98
00:03:54,777 --> 00:03:55,903
Good choice.

99
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:58,364
Popular car, dark color.

100
00:03:58,447 --> 00:03:59,448
We won't stand out.

101
00:03:59,531 --> 00:04:01,700
So glad I'm a good car thief.

102
00:04:01,784 --> 00:04:02,743
[Reacher] Head to D.C.

103
00:04:04,119 --> 00:04:06,163
-Plum's loft?
-Feds and local cops will have

104
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:07,623
pulled the place apart by now.

105
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:10,250
Plum's in the hospital.
We'd have no reason to go back.

106
00:04:10,334 --> 00:04:11,919
Last place anyone would look.

107
00:04:12,002 --> 00:04:13,712
Keep it under 70.

108
00:04:13,796 --> 00:04:15,631
We get pulled over, we have a problem.

109
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:16,715
Copy that.

110
00:04:23,055 --> 00:04:25,182
[weatherman] ...multiple inches
of rain per hour,

111
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,559
with even heavier downpours overnight.

112
00:04:27,643 --> 00:04:30,229
We're also tracking
a high number of lightning strikes

113
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:32,314
within the leading edge of the system,

114
00:04:32,398 --> 00:04:33,816
and that's expected to increase

115
00:04:33,899 --> 00:04:35,734
as the storm approaches the city.

116
00:04:35,818 --> 00:04:37,403
-[groans]
-We'll continue updating this

117
00:04:37,486 --> 00:04:38,988
throughout the evening, so keep it here

118
00:04:39,071 --> 00:04:42,741
as we track tonight's
unseasonably strong summer storm.

119
00:04:42,825 --> 00:04:44,451
-[news program theme plays]
-Oh, shit.

120
00:04:44,535 --> 00:04:46,245
[news anchor] Just in,
we have more on the attack

121
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:48,080
that killed North Carolina representative

122
00:04:48,163 --> 00:04:52,084
and recently-announced
presidential candidate John Sampson.

123
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:54,253
-Shit.
-A camera crew covering

124
00:04:54,336 --> 00:04:56,839
the Feed America event at the waterfront

125
00:04:56,922 --> 00:04:58,382
caught this footage

126
00:04:58,465 --> 00:04:59,591
-of Congressman Sampson...
-[straining]

127
00:04:59,675 --> 00:05:02,636
...tackling the suicide bomber
into the water...

128
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,388
-[grunts in relief]
-...sacrificing himself

129
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:06,265
to save countless lives.

130
00:05:06,348 --> 00:05:09,059
We caution that
this footage is disturbing.

131
00:05:09,143 --> 00:05:10,602
[indistinct chatter]

132
00:05:10,686 --> 00:05:12,813
[Sampson yelling]

133
00:05:13,522 --> 00:05:14,398
[loud splash]

134
00:05:14,481 --> 00:05:15,357
[explosion]

135
00:05:15,441 --> 00:05:17,026
[people screaming]

136
00:05:17,109 --> 00:05:19,403
[news anchor] Congressman Sampson's
widow, Elspeth Sampson,

137
00:05:19,486 --> 00:05:21,613
is asking that anyone with information

138
00:05:21,697 --> 00:05:24,491
about this man, or his accomplices,

139
00:05:24,575 --> 00:05:26,243
to please reach out directly

140
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:29,580
to Congressman Sampson's
head of security at this number.

141
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:31,331
[tense, percussive music playing]

142
00:05:31,415 --> 00:05:33,125
"Tomas Waberi."

143
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:36,628
[groaning softly]

144
00:05:45,137 --> 00:05:46,638
[straining]

145
00:05:49,767 --> 00:05:52,227
[panting]

146
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:54,772
-[groaning]
-[monitor beeping]

147
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:58,358
[panting]

148
00:05:58,442 --> 00:06:00,527
[groaning]

149
00:06:06,075 --> 00:06:07,367
Oh...

150
00:06:10,621 --> 00:06:11,705
Okay.

151
00:06:13,165 --> 00:06:14,666
[groans]

152
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:15,793
[yells]

153
00:06:15,876 --> 00:06:16,877
Shit.

154
00:06:18,295 --> 00:06:19,338
Okay.

155
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:22,966
[groans softly]

156
00:06:23,050 --> 00:06:24,551
[panting]

157
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:28,180
[grunts, yells]

158
00:06:29,264 --> 00:06:30,641
[groaning]

159
00:06:30,724 --> 00:06:31,809
The fuck?

160
00:06:31,892 --> 00:06:33,060
Excuse me.

161
00:06:33,143 --> 00:06:34,728
Help me to get him into bed.

162
00:06:34,812 --> 00:06:36,688
[Russell groaning loudly]

163
00:06:36,772 --> 00:06:38,899
You just had surgery.
What in God's name

164
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:41,276
-were you trying to do?
-[groaning]

165
00:06:49,535 --> 00:06:50,452
Who you trying to call?

166
00:06:50,536 --> 00:06:51,745
[groans]

167
00:06:51,829 --> 00:06:53,705
[panting]

168
00:06:53,789 --> 00:06:55,374
[Docherty] I ain't on
the wrong side of all this.

169
00:06:55,457 --> 00:06:58,502
Jacob Merrick asked me
to come here and check on you.

170
00:06:58,585 --> 00:07:00,671
He said he's sorry
he left you at the library,

171
00:07:00,754 --> 00:07:02,756
whatever the fuck that means.

172
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:04,133
What's going on?

173
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:05,926
[labored breathing]

174
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:08,095
[faintly] Tomas... Waberi.

175
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:09,429
You were trying to call him?

176
00:07:09,513 --> 00:07:11,849
No. That's...

177
00:07:11,932 --> 00:07:14,351
the suici... [wheezes]

178
00:07:14,434 --> 00:07:15,811
...suicide bomber.

179
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:18,647
[groaning]

180
00:07:18,730 --> 00:07:19,815
Are you sure about that?

181
00:07:19,898 --> 00:07:20,941
I'm sure.

182
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,234
I'm s-- [groans]

183
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:23,235
[Docherty] Okay.

184
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:24,862
-I'll take it from here.
-Okay.

185
00:07:25,904 --> 00:07:27,322
You did good, Plum.

186
00:07:27,406 --> 00:07:28,282
[Russell exhales]

187
00:07:28,365 --> 00:07:30,742
[whimpers, groans]

188
00:07:34,246 --> 00:07:36,248
[intense music playing]

189
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:38,167
[sirens wailing]

190
00:07:42,546 --> 00:07:43,672
[SWAT officer] Clear!

191
00:07:45,257 --> 00:07:46,300
[SWAT officer 2] Clear!

192
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:47,718
-[SWAT officer 3] Clear!
-Damn.

193
00:07:47,801 --> 00:07:48,844
[SWAT officer 4] Clear!

194
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:50,012
[SWAT officer] Clear!

195
00:07:50,095 --> 00:07:52,014
[indistinct radio chatter]

196
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:54,808
Shit.

197
00:07:58,312 --> 00:08:00,314
[phone ringing]

198
00:08:03,609 --> 00:08:04,776
Docherty, what up?

199
00:08:04,860 --> 00:08:07,571
Your boy Plum pointed us
to the guy who killed Sampson.

200
00:08:07,654 --> 00:08:08,822
Russell's okay?

201
00:08:08,906 --> 00:08:10,866
He's jacked up, but alive.

202
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:12,367
Nearly ripped himself apart

203
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:15,287
trying to get us the name of the bomber,
Tomas Waberi.

204
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:17,748
Now, we ran it down.
He rented a car when he landed.

205
00:08:17,831 --> 00:08:21,501
Rental agency used GPS
to trace it to a warehouse.

206
00:08:21,585 --> 00:08:24,129
Car was in the lot, but place was empty.

207
00:08:24,213 --> 00:08:25,714
Only thing they left behind was

208
00:08:25,797 --> 00:08:27,925
a sealed, 45-gallon drum

209
00:08:28,008 --> 00:08:29,509
with a dead kid inside.

210
00:08:29,593 --> 00:08:31,220
Never seen anything like it.

211
00:08:31,303 --> 00:08:32,888
They tested the toxin on him.

212
00:08:32,971 --> 00:08:34,598
Anything pointing to where they went?

213
00:08:34,681 --> 00:08:37,935
Credit card that bought
Waberi's plane ticket picked up 13 more

214
00:08:38,018 --> 00:08:39,728
for a red-eye tonight,

215
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:42,147
two first class, 11 coach.

216
00:08:42,231 --> 00:08:43,649
Lila and Amisha are first class.

217
00:08:44,483 --> 00:08:46,360
The other 11,
figure a computer expert,

218
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:49,488
a chemist,
maybe an explosives guy to rig the vest.

219
00:08:49,571 --> 00:08:51,073
The rest are trained killers.

220
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:53,242
Reinforcements brought in
when things went to hell.

221
00:08:53,325 --> 00:08:55,619
[Docherty] Well, we're tracking down
the names they'll be flying under.

222
00:08:55,702 --> 00:08:57,579
It's gonna be all hands on deck at PHL.

223
00:08:57,663 --> 00:08:58,622
They won't show.

224
00:08:59,456 --> 00:09:01,250
-Why not?
-'Cause the attack failed.

225
00:09:01,333 --> 00:09:03,669
They didn't prove to bidders
their chemical weapon works.

226
00:09:03,752 --> 00:09:05,963
Tell that to fish in the Delaware.

227
00:09:06,046 --> 00:09:08,215
Better yet, tell that to John Sampson.

228
00:09:08,298 --> 00:09:10,676
Trust me,
these assholes proved their point.

229
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:12,678
Their point was to demonstrate
a chemical weapon

230
00:09:12,761 --> 00:09:14,846
that's effectively lethal outdoors.

231
00:09:14,930 --> 00:09:16,098
They aren't going anywhere.

232
00:09:16,181 --> 00:09:17,683
[Docherty] They got what they came for.

233
00:09:17,766 --> 00:09:20,435
All that's left for them is
to get out of Dodge and cash in.

234
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:22,938
When they arrive at the airport,
we'll be waiting.

235
00:09:23,021 --> 00:09:25,899
Just keep your heads down
until we got 'em in custody.

236
00:09:25,983 --> 00:09:28,485
You were there
when a congressman exploded.

237
00:09:28,568 --> 00:09:30,779
Everyone thinks you're working with 'em.

238
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,698
-Don't be a fucking hero.
-[phone beeps off]

239
00:09:37,661 --> 00:09:39,830
Are you 100% on Lila
and Amisha not running off?

240
00:09:39,913 --> 00:09:40,831
Pretty much.

241
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,207
Well, we need to find them,

242
00:09:42,291 --> 00:09:43,458
'cause the cops aren't looking.

243
00:09:43,542 --> 00:09:44,918
They could be anywhere.

244
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,963
Not anywhere.

245
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:49,631
They need somewhere
they can cook the poison.

246
00:09:49,715 --> 00:09:51,675
Somewhere they can pivot to quickly,

247
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,385
a place no one would think they'd go.

248
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,511
[tense music playing]

249
00:09:54,594 --> 00:09:55,637
Fuck.

250
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:58,890
They're doing what we're doing.

251
00:09:58,974 --> 00:10:00,809
Circling back to where
the cops already looked.

252
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,520
The vacant restaurant building?

253
00:10:03,603 --> 00:10:04,896
Turn around.

254
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:07,482
♪ ♪

255
00:10:15,824 --> 00:10:17,826
[tense, ominous music playing]

256
00:10:23,749 --> 00:10:25,751
[quiet chatter]

257
00:10:39,598 --> 00:10:40,891
First batch is good.

258
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:43,018
Another hour and we'll have what we need.

259
00:10:43,643 --> 00:10:45,270
Great.

260
00:10:45,354 --> 00:10:47,314
Can't let Amisha down, yeah?

261
00:10:51,902 --> 00:10:53,904
♪ ♪

262
00:11:08,668 --> 00:11:10,504
[in Indonesian] One hour.

263
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:11,380
Any luck?

264
00:11:11,463 --> 00:11:16,760
Crop duster rental 25 miles
